From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NP <50584693+NatePu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:50:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] T1.0: build integration for pseudo-device flow

- sys/conf/files: pseudo-device flow, file net/if_flow.c (needs-flag).
- sys/conf/GENERIC: pseudo-device flow (amd64 and octeon include it).
- arch/octeon/conf/files.octeon: if_cnmac_flow.c for "flow & cnmac".
- net/if_flow.h: hook API of DESIGN 3.1; empty inline stubs when
  NFLOW == 0; refuses to compile without "flow.h".
- net/if_flowvar.h: flow key, struct flow, MD ops (ERRATA E80).
- net/if_flow.c: flowattach() sets up the pool, buckets, SipHash key,
  counters, kstat flow:0:stats, closed gates, the GC timeout and the
  single-worker flow_tq.
- arch/octeon/dev/if_cnmac_flow.c: placeholder for the MD glue.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
